al Medley, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2001824"} "4 × 100 metres Medley Relay, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2001829"} "4 × 100 metres Medley Relay, Mixed"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "5421"} "1956"] "\n" [:option {:value "5544"} "1960"] "\n" [:option {:value "5710"} "1964"] "\n" [:option {:value "5949"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "6265"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "6563"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "6821"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "7055"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "7372"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "7728"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "8075"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "8466"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "8866"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "261601"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "322143"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "357100"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19000129"} "2020"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/578"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "200 metres Butterfly, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "30 – 31 July 2024"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2158"} "Paris La Défense Arena, Nanterre, France"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/2001636"} "27 from 22 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The defending gold medalist was Hungarian " [:a {:href "/athletes/2503191"} "Kristóf Milák"] " and he was back, but the favorite was the Frenchman " [:a {:href "/athletes/142925"} "Léon Marchand"] ", who had already won the 400 individual medley in Paris, three days before this final. Further, Marchand was attempting what some considered a crazy double on this day. He would swim the final of the 200 metre breaststroke about two hours after this race would end."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Milák and Marchand led the semi-final qualifiers, in that order, and the final was all about them, as the bronze medalist Canada’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/154417"} "Ilya Kharun"] " would be over a second back of silver."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Milák went out fastest, leading through the first three turns, and had a comfortable lead on Marchand at that point. But Marchand’s furious finish would bring him home for the gold medal, outsplitting Milák on the final lap by 1.26 seconds."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Two hours after this race, Marchand would return and win gold in the 200 breaststroke, completing a rare double by a male swimmer. It had been done in 1896 by Hungary’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/48186"} "Alfréd Hajós"] " and in 1900 by Australian/Brit " [:a {:href "/athletes/45233"} "Fred Lane"] ", but since then only by East Germany’s female " [:a {:href "/athletes/47465"} "Kornelia Ender"] ", who won the 200 metre freestyle and 100 metre butterfly at the same session in 1988."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Two days later, Marchand would win another gold in the 200 individual medley, becoming only the third male swimmer, after " [:a {:href "/athletes/93860"} "Michael Phelps"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/51572"} "Mark Spitz"] ", to win four individual swimming gold medals at a single Olympic Games. Marchand was the only athlete at Paris 2024 to win four gold medals, in any sport, and he also added a bronze in the men’s medley relay."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/142925"} "Léon Marchand"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-ri